          "The review below covers renewal risk evidence only for accounts that reached the ninety-day checkpoint during the observation window during a single stated window. It is an internal check on what the record can support, not a benchmark or an audit opinion. A reader should be able to tell which cases were eligible and which were left out. That clarity matters more than a tidy percentage at the top of the page.",
          "Set the boundary of this renewal risk evidence check before anyone opens a case. Name the opening event, the ending event, and the conditions that pause the clock. Without those three pieces, a count reflects whoever happened to be working that week. CustomerSuccessManagers writes the boundary into the working file so a second reviewer can apply it unchanged. The next owner should be able to see which fields were checked and which were left open.",
