          "Draw the population line before selecting the first case. List every exclusion with a reason, including accounts that changed owner during the window. Picking cases from the easiest queue will flatter any control. The goal is an honest picture of the work that actually arrived, not a polished sample. Keep the note short enough to read during a live account review and specific enough to be tested later.",
          "The counting unit is one account crossing its ninety-day renewal checkpoint. Try that definition on three awkward cases before accepting it: one shared owner, one still open, and one reopened. Every case in the extract must meet the same test or be listed as an exclusion. A unit that shifts mid-window makes month-over-month comparison meaningless. Do not merge the item into the account summary until the supporting source is attached."
