          "Write the definition of done before the sample is drawn. Here, done means a dated source and a named reviewer support the measure for that case. A tracker that says closed does not override a missing source. CustomerSuccessManagers keeps the tracker value and the evidence side by side so the gap is obvious. Do not merge the item into the account summary until the supporting source is attached.",
          "Each case carries four fields: source, observation time, the field it supports, and the reviewer. Treat missing, unavailable, and confirmed-negative as three separate values. Merging them hides whether evidence was absent or simply not collected. Agree the value list in advance so the extract does not drift after the first interesting result. A monthly sample will show whether the rule survives a busy week with partial coverage."
