          "Each adoption data freshness case needs a pointer to the system where the work really lives. Usually that is the customer success platform, the support queue, or the billing record, not a side spreadsheet. A secondary tracker is fine when it refreshes from the source and shows its age. CustomerSuccessManagers treats an uncited row as a lead to verify, never as evidence.",
          "Access belongs inside the evidence rule for adoption data freshness. If a reviewer cannot open the source, a screenshot is a poor substitute for the record. Use named accounts with the least permission the review needs, and revoke them when the assignment ends. CustomerSuccessManagers counts access failures as findings so the sample does not drift toward easy cases. Escalate the pattern, not only the individual case, when the same gap appears twice in a row.",
          "Retention policy determines how long a adoption data freshness record can answer a later question. Keep source, decision, and close note for the approved period, and leave sensitive detail in the approved system. The reviewer should know which fields are restricted before the first observation. CustomerSuccessManagers records only a reference in the working file when the underlying content is restricted."
